WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.434
-You look good, man.
You're a stud.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.434
-Alright, alright.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.434
-Come on,
Travis Kelce in the house.

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:06.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.400
-How we doing, guys? Man.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.067
-Couldn't have happened to
a better dude, man.

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:11.567
-This is
a dream come true, Jimmy.

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:12.734
This is sweet.
-Come on, bud.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.033
-Are you kidding me?

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:16.734
-We met each other probably
almost a year ago, right?

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:19.267
-Yeah, just about a year ago.
Vegas, baby. Vegas.

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.467
-We were at -- Justin Timberlake
had a golf tournament.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.367
-Mm-hmm.
-8:00 a.m. golf tournament.

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:25.667
-Yeah, 8:00 a.m. golf tourney.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:28.567
-And we play -- And we never met
each other, hung out.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:31.334
We hung out all day and we
totally hit it off, I thought.

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:32.901
-I couldn't
get away from you, man.

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:34.567
-I know. I was kind of a fanboy.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.367
I kept following you around
like, "Hey, Travis.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.534
Hi, bud. Hi, man."
Yeah, exactly.

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.701
-My favorite part
was "Mustang Sally," baby.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:42.934
-Oh, dude.

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:44.534
-He jumped up on the stage
and gave us all --

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:46.567
-We had to rock it out.
We had to scream.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.334
I was going nuts.
But, dude, we were hanging out.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:49.567
You were so fun.

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.834
I've got to say --
How does it feel now?

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:54.100
This is the second time
you won the Super Bowl, bud.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.968
-Man, I'll tell you what --
the first time

00:00:55.968 --> 00:01:00.534
was one of the most emotional
like, "I finally did it."

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:02.067
-Yeah. Yeah, exactly. Yeah.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:05.400
-And then we lost to
the Tampa Bay Buccaneers,

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.033
got our tails whupped
pretty good against them.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:09.200
So that was a low moment.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.167
And then it kind of
build back up.

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:13.834
And to get this one, to be back
on the mountaintop, man,

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:15.267
I'll tell you what, it's
the best feeling in the world.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:17.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, buddy.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.868
You were so good.
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:21.300
Especially to do it with
the guys we did it with,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.968
the ups and downs through it,
the adversity of the season.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.100
It was a lot of fun, man.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.734
-But also to do it with
Patrick Mahomes.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.334
That's where I met you.
You guys were together.

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:30.801
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:33.701
-Was that a plan for you guys
to hang out on the off-season

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.100
and be kind of best friends.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.334
-I think it just
happened organically.

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:39.801
It was just like, "Hey, man,
what are you doing?

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:41.300
You're about to go to Vegas
and play golf?

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.601
Alright, let's do it."
-Really?

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:46.801
-And it's been awesome since
he's been in Kansas City.

00:01:46.801 --> 00:01:49.968
He doesn't get enough credit for
the type of leader that he is,

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:53.567
the type of just personable guy
he is in the locker room.

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:56.234
And it's on and off the field.

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:58.834
He does unbelievable things
in the community in Kansas City.

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:00.734
And that's the kind of,
you know,

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:02.467
vibe that I like
to be around, man.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:03.901
-Yeah.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.767
-And it was just kind of like
magnets when he got to K.C.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.100
-Yeah, but I --
'Cause I was thinking,

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.501
"Oh, maybe this is a plan.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:11.968
Maybe Andy Reid said, 'Hey,
you guys should be best friends.

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:13.300
Just go play with each other.'"

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.834
-Just compete and --
-Go to a movie.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.200
Go to a movie, go do something,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.834
go watch Netflix for an
afternoon or something, yeah.

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:22.100
-It started with the,
"Hey, do you drink beers?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.667
Do you drink beer?"
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:25.567
-Because I like to drink beers.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.501
-It sounds like
we could have some fun.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:28.901
-Yeah, exactly.
And you guys bonded.

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.033
I just thought it was great,
and you have great chemistry

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:31.133
and it's real.

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:32.634
It's not fake at all.

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:36.434
I witnessed it for a weekend.
It was, like, so cool to watch.

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:37.968
The parade was yesterday.
-Yes.

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:39.367
-So I want to thank you
for being here today.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:40.767
-Oh, man,
I almost didn't make it.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:43.701
-I know, I know, I know, I know,
I know, I know, I know.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.000
I was actually --
I was thinking about --

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.868
I was going to call Jason
if you didn't show up.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.601
I'm like, "Dude, get over here.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:53.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
Jason, get over here right now."

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:55.801
Everyone's always
asking about your brother.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:58.000
But that must have been just
a bizarre thing

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.100
to be playing in the Super Bowl
with your brother.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:04.801
-Man, it was -- You know,
you always dream growing up that

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.434
you're going to one day
be in the Super Bowl,

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:10.167
especially when my brother's the
reason why I even play football.

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:11.601
Like -- Yeah, exactly.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:14.300
When I was growing up -- I'm two
years younger than my brother.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:18.400
And that's about as drunk as
I was at the parade right there.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.634
That's me

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:20.634
-That's during
the parade yesterday?

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:21.868
-Yeah, that's me.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.033
That's full parade form
right there.

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:24.267
-Oh, my God.

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:25.501
I thought this was when
you were a kid.

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:27.767
This is yesterday.
-No, this is yesterday.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:28.868
Yeah, growing up in
Cleveland, Ohio,

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:31.534
I followed his footsteps
in a lot of areas,

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:33.567
sports being one of them
and football

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:35.334
definitely being one of them.

00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:38.000
And you always imagine, you
know, playing on the same team,

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.000
but, man, I'll tell you what,
the way the football world

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.701
and everybody embraced my family
and me and my brother

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:45.067
playing against each other --

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:46.300
for the first time, two brothers
playing against each other

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.601
in the Super Bowl.

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:50.334
It was cool to break
that barrier and see my family

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:51.834
and all the light
and getting all the glory.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:53.133
Man, it was beautiful.

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:54.567
-I mean, 'cause when you were a
kid, like there --

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.400
You're probably in your front
yard or something?

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.934
-Yeah, probably
3 or 5 years old, maybe.

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.234
-Yeah, and what's
the big Super Bowl there?

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:02.601
Like, you're like --
I don't know what it is.

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:04.300
Like, Thanksgiving?
-Exactly.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.367
-Like a Turkey Bowl
or something?

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:06.400
-Exactly.
-Yeah.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.200
-Just excited we got costumes

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.033
and we can look like
football players.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:11.133
-Yeah. Here's you
and your brother

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:12.200
at this year's Super Bowl.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.400
-Alright, now.
-Yeah.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.701
All the cameras
got you right there saying,

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:16.868
"Hey, I love you, bro."

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:18.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.033
And I also got to give
a shout-out.

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:24.000
Your mom has been the cutest
for this whole ride,

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.334
'cause everyone is like,
"Who are you rooting for?

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.167
What son do you like better?"
You know, all that stuff.

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.601
And she's been so cool.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.000
And I've got to show you
the jacket.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.167
Here's what Mama Kelce
was wearing.

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:33.367
-Split right down the middle
right there.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:35.434
-Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:39.234
You see the red side's
on that left right there.

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:40.367
-Yeah.

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:41.501
-It's right there
next to that heart.

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:44.501
She knows. Mama knows best.
Mama knows best.

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:46.133
-I mean, mama knows best.

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.467
-That right shoe looked way
better than the left shoe.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.400
No offense, guys.
No offense, guys.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.834
-I know this is tough for
The Roots to be --

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:53.133
'Cause they're just such
Philly fans.

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:57.601
But you know what?
No one picked -- Look at this.

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.801
No one picked you guys to win at
all, none of the experts.

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.767
-The experts.
-The experts.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:04.400
-The experts say that, yeah,
the Chiefs were out of it

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.601
way back in April, I think.

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:09.767
We lost a
big-name wide receiver,

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:12.934
one of my favorite teammates
ever, Tyreek Hill,

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:15.734
and they thought that it
was just -- it was over for us.

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:18.167
And that's why being on
that mountaintop, man,

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:19.968
it just felt
that much sweeter, man.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:24.167
-But did you feel --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:27.767
'Cause watching the Super Bowl,
I thought you were out.

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:28.901
I've got to be honest.

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:30.234
I mean, that second half

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:31.634
and when Patrick
started limping off the field,

00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:32.767
I go, "Oh, gosh."

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:33.868
-10-point lead, man.

00:05:33.868 --> 00:05:36.000
Don't give Pat Mahomes
10 points,

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.501
because he will just floor it.

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:39.501
-Really?
He's like, "Don't tell me no."

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:42.200
-Yeah, he got --
It will probably go down

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.834
as one of my favorite speeches.

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:46.767
At halftime,
he got electric, man.

00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:50.534
He lit a fire in everybody's
tail just to, you know,

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:52.734
want it that much more.

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:55.300
And when you can do that
with a group of men, man,

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:56.734
that's a special human being
right there.

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:58.267
-Yeah, and you got everyone
hyped up and you came back.

00:05:58.267 --> 00:05:59.734
It was an unbelievable comeback.

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:01.367
-Second half
was a lot of energy, man.

00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:02.734
A lot of energy.
A lot of passion.

00:06:02.734 --> 00:06:04.400
-We have a big announcement that

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.634
we're going to announce here
on the show tonight.

00:06:05.634 --> 00:06:07.033
I'm very excited about this.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:09.267
You're going to be back
in our building in a few weeks.

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:10.334
Can you say why
you're coming back?

00:06:10.334 --> 00:06:11.467
-Yeah, for sure.

00:06:11.467 --> 00:06:14.300
I mean, growing up,
I was a huge, like,

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:19.734
Farley, Ferrell, Fallon
kind of guy growing up.

00:06:19.734 --> 00:06:22.767
And, yeah, I used to watch
"Saturday Night Live"

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:23.934
with my mother.

00:06:23.934 --> 00:06:27.100
And it's an absolute honor
and a privilege

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.701
to be hosting "SNL" March 4th.

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:31.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:35.367
-Come on, buddy!
Come on, bud! Yes!

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:38.868
It's going to be great!
It's going to be great!

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:40.767
-I am so nervous for that.
Oh, my gosh.

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:43.801
-You are going to be so good.
I was talking to Lorne today.

00:06:43.801 --> 00:06:46.667
I'm like, "Oh, he's so charming
and he can sing and he's fun."

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:48.801
And it's so good.
-You think that about me?

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:50.667
-I do. Yeah.
-Thanks, man.

00:06:50.667 --> 00:06:52.667
-I know. Yeah, yeah. I do.

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:55.734
-You're making me blush, man.
-Oh, it's amazing.

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:58.067
But Kelsea Ballerini
is musical guest.

00:06:58.067 --> 00:07:00.300
-Yes. Yes.
-So it's going to be a hot show.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.033
Congratulations on that.
-Thank you very much.

00:07:02.033 --> 00:07:03.901
-You know, it's interesting
that -- I was just --

00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:05.501
It's interesting that
I brought up singing,

00:07:05.501 --> 00:07:08.968
because I know that you
do some karaoke.

00:07:08.968 --> 00:07:11.200
And --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.167
-How did you know?

00:07:13.167 --> 00:07:16.133
-It's kind of out there.
-How'd it get out there?

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:18.567
-There was one song that has
been very important to you

00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:21.067
during this playoff run,
and I thought maybe,

00:07:21.067 --> 00:07:22.767
if we can convince you...

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:24.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
We've got The Roots.

00:07:24.934 --> 00:07:26.534
We've got the best in
the business right there.

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:27.934
-Fellas, do you mind?

00:07:27.934 --> 00:07:29.968
♪♪
Kick it!

00:07:29.968 --> 00:07:31.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:07:35.501 --> 00:07:37.767
Whoo!

00:07:37.767 --> 00:07:42.100
